              -	Encryption null
              -	Security-protocol noauth
              -	Encrypted noauth

              e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
              If 'strong-password max-length' is displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

              f)	The validity period of an account can be configured.

              NOTE: password complexity (either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4) and/or strong-password-info is not configured."
              solution    : "It is recommended to set password consists of digits, letters, and symbols

              ZXR10# configure terminal
              ZXR10 (config)# system-user
              ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password length 8 character number capital lowercase special-character"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </else>
        </if>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - c) Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password - strong-password dictionary"
          info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

          a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

          b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

          c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

          d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
          -	Encrypt none
          -	Authentication null
          -	Encrypted null
          -	Encryption null
          -	Security-protocol noauth
          -	Encrypted noauth

          e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
          If 'strong-password max-length' is displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

          f)	The validity period of an account can be configured."
          solution    : "It is recommended to set password to support check of simple passwords and weak passwords

          ZXR10# configure terminal
          ZXR10 (config)# system-user
          ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password dictionary"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          expect      : ".*strong-password dictionary"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - c) Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password - same-consecutive"
          info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

          a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

          b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

          c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

          d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
          -	Encrypt none
          -	Authentication null
          -	Encrypted null
          -	Encryption null
          -	Security-protocol noauth
          -	Encrypted noauth

          e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
          If 'strong-password max-length' is displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

          f)	The validity period of an account can be configured."
          solution    : "It is recommended to set password to support check of simple passwords and weak passwords

          ZXR10# configure terminal
          ZXR10 (config)# system-user
          ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password same-consecutive 5"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          expect      : ".*strong-password same-consecutive .+"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - d) Display password in cipher text"
          info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

          a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

          b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

          c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

          d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
          -	Encrypt none
          -	Authentication null
          -	Encrypted null
          -	Encryption null
          -	Security-protocol noauth
          -	Encrypted noauth

          e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
          If 'strong-password max-length' is displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

          f)	The validity period of an account can be configured."
          solution    : "It is recommended config to support stores passwords in ciphertext, do not include the following phrases in the configuration:

          - encrypt none
          - authentication null
          - encrypted null
          - encryption null
          - security-protocol noauth
          - encrypted noauth"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          not_expect  : "(encrypt none|(authentication|encrypted|encryption) null|(security-protocol|encrypted) noauth)"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - e) Check for strong-password username-related-chk inverse"
          info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

          a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

          b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

          c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

          d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
          -	Encrypt none
          -	Authentication null
          -	Encrypted null
          -	Encryption null
          -	Security-protocol noauth
          -	Encrypted noauth

          e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
          If 'strong-password max-length' displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

          f)	The validity period of an account can be configured."
          solution    : "It is recommended to set the password to irrelevant to the username and date.

          ZXR10# configure terminal
          ZXR10 (config)# system-user
          ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password username-related-chk inverse"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          expect      : ".*strong-password username-related-chk"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - e) Check for strong-password date-check enable"
          info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

          a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

          b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

          c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

          d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
          -	Encrypt none
          -	Authentication null
          -	Encrypted null
          -	Encryption null
          -	Security-protocol noauth
          -	Encrypted noauth

          e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
          If 'strong-password max-length' displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

          f)	The validity period of an account can be configured."
          solution    : "It is recommended to set the password to irrelevant to the username and date.

          ZXR10# configure terminal
          ZXR10 (config)# system-user
          ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password date-check enable"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          expect      : ".*strong-password date-check enable"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - f) The validity period of an account can be configured"
          info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

          a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

          b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

          c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

          d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
          -	Encrypt none
          -	Authentication null
          -	Encrypted null
          -	Encryption null
          -	Security-protocol noauth
          -	Encrypted noauth

          e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
          If 'strong-password max-length' displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

          f)	The validity period of an account can be configured."
          solution    : "It is recommended to set the password validity period

          ZXR10# configure terminal
          ZXR10 (config)# system-user
          ZXR10 (config-system-user)# user-name xxx
          ZXR10 (config-system-user-username)# password-duration 360"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          expect      : "[^\\r\\n]*password-duration ([1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|[1-2][0-9][0-9]|[3][0-5][0-9]|360)"
        </custom_item>
      </else>
    </if>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Check if strong-password check has been disabled"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          expect      : "strong-password check disable"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"WARNING">
          description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - e) Check for strong-password max-length"
          info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

          a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

          b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

          c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

          d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
          -	Encrypt none
          -	Authentication null
          -	Encrypted null
          -	Encryption null
          -	Security-protocol noauth
          -	Encrypted noauth

          e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
          If 'strong-password max-length' is displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

          f)	The validity period of an account can be configured.

          NOTE: strong-password check disable has been configured.

          NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
          solution    : "It is recommended to set the maximum password length to at least 10

          ZXR10# configure terminal
          ZXR10 (config)# system-user
          ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password max-length 64"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <if>
          <condition type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type        : CMD_EXEC
              description : "Check if strong-password max-length is configured"
              cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
              expect      : ".*strong-password max-length.*"
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <custom_item>
              type        : CMD_EXEC
              description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - e) Check for strong-password max-length"
              info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

              a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

              b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

              c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

              d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
              -	Encrypt none
              -	Authentication null
              -	Encrypted null
              -	Encryption null
              -	Security-protocol noauth
              -	Encrypted noauth

              e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
              If 'strong-password max-length' is displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

              f)	The validity period of an account can be configured."
              solution    : "It is recommended to set the maximum password length to at least 10

              ZXR10# configure terminal
              ZXR10 (config)# system-user
              ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password max-length 64"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
              expect      : ".*strong-password max-length [1-9][0-9]{1,2}"
            </custom_item>
          </then>

          <else>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.2 Password Security Policy - e) Check for strong-password max-length"
              info        : "Strong passwords are supported to prevent passwords from being cracked. When a password is set, password complexity is detected by default. If a password does not meet the policy, a warning is required. A strong password mode should be provided. The password verification mechanism is as follows:

              a)	The default password length shouldn't be below 8 characters.

              b)	The password must include either three of 'number', 'capital', 'lowercase', 'special-character' or set the 'character-set-num' value to 3-4

              c)	Configure 'strong-password dictionary' and 'same-consecutive' to avoid weak password

              d)	Display password in cipher text. Check either of the following words exist in configuration file:
              -	Encrypt none
              -	Authentication null
              -	Encrypted null
              -	Encryption null
              -	Security-protocol noauth
              -	Encrypted noauth

              e)	If 'strong-password max-length' is not displayed in configuration, then pass this check.
              If 'strong-password max-length' is displayed in configuration, but max-length value below 10, or not both configuration 'username-related-chk inverse' and 'strong-password date-check enable' commands, then fail this check.

              f)	The validity period of an account can be configured.

              NOTE: strong-password max-length has not been configured."
              solution    : "It is recommended to set the maximum password length to at least 10

              ZXR10# configure terminal
              ZXR10 (config)# system-user
              ZXR10 (config-system-user)# strong-password max-length 64"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </else>
        </if>
      </else>
    </if>

# 7.3 (1.3)  SEC-SYS-GEN-030 Account Anti-riot Attack

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Check if user-authen-restriction is configured"
          cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
          expect      : ".*user-authen-restriction"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
#user-authen-restriction is configured

        <if>
          <condition type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type        : CMD_EXEC
              description : "Check if user-authen-restriction - fail-time and lock-minute is configured"
              cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
              expect      : ".*user-authen-restriction.+fail-time.+lock-minute.+"
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
#Check if fail-time is 0

            <if>
              <condition type:"AND">
                <custom_item>
                  type        : CMD_EXEC
                  description : "Check if user-authen-restriction - fail-time is 0"
                  cmd         : "show running-config system-user all"
                  expect      : ".*user-authen-restriction.+fail-time 0 lock-minute.+"
                </custom_item>
              </condition>

              <then>
#fail-time is 0

                <report type:"FAILED">
                  description : "1.3 Account Anti-riot Attack"
                  info        : "Some tools exist on the Internet, which specifically attack the management-plane protocol accounts of the system and frequently attempt accounts to attack devices so as to obtain accounts. Therefore, the system should be able to reject all remote login requests in a blocking manner when it is found that repeated remote login attempts fail for a certain number of consecutive times by monitoring the system account authentication. At this time, only IP requests from whitelisted users are allowed to be responded). This blocking can last for a period of time, so as to achieve the purpose of timely cutting off brute-force cracking attempts and protecting the CPU processing capability of the management plane.

                  NOTE: fail-time is set to 0"
                  solution    : "Configuring the number of failures and locking time by running the following commands:

                  ZXR10 (config)#system-user
                  ZXR10 (config-system-user)#user-authen-restriction fail-time 3 lock-minute 2"
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>
              </then>

              <else>
#fail-time is not 0

                <report type:"PASSED">
                  description : "1.3 Account Anti-riot Attack"
                  info        : "Some tools exist on the Internet, which specifically attack the management-plane protocol accounts of the system and frequently attempt accounts to attack devices so as to obtain accounts. Therefore, the system should be able to reject all remote login requests in a blocking manner when it is found that repeated remote login attempts fail for a certain number of consecutive times by monitoring the system account authentication. At this time, only IP requests from whitelisted users are allowed to be responded). This blocking can last for a period of time, so as to achieve the purpose of timely cutting off brute-force cracking attempts and protecting the CPU processing capability of the management plane."
                  solution    : "Configuring the number of failures and locking time by running the following commands:

                  ZXR10 (config)#system-user
                  ZXR10 (config-system-user)#user-authen-restriction fail-time 3 lock-minute 2"
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>
              </else>
            </if>
          </then>

          <else>
#fail-time and/or lock-minute not configured

            <report type:"FAILED">
              description : "1.3 Account Anti-riot Attack"
              info        : "Some tools exist on the Internet, which specifically attack the management-plane protocol accounts of the system and frequently attempt accounts to attack devices so as to obtain accounts. Therefore, the system should be able to reject all remote login requests in a blocking manner when it is found that repeated remote login attempts fail for a certain number of consecutive times by monitoring the system account authentication. At this time, only IP requests from whitelisted users are allowed to be responded). This blocking can last for a period of time, so as to achieve the purpose of timely cutting off brute-force cracking attempts and protecting the CPU processing capability of the management plane.

              NOTE: Either fail-time and/or lock-minute not configured."
              solution    : "Configuring the number of failures and locking time by running the following commands:

              ZXR10 (config)#system-user
              ZXR10 (config-system-user)#user-authen-restriction fail-time 3 lock-minute 2"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </else>
        </if>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.3 Account Anti-riot Attack"
          info        : "Some tools exist on the Internet, which specifically attack the management-plane protocol accounts of the system and frequently attempt accounts to attack devices so as to obtain accounts. Therefore, the system should be able to reject all remote login requests in a blocking manner when it is found that repeated remote login attempts fail for a certain number of consecutive times by monitoring the system account authentication. At this time, only IP requests from whitelisted users are allowed to be responded). This blocking can last for a period of time, so as to achieve the purpose of timely cutting off brute-force cracking attempts and protecting the CPU processing capability of the management plane.

          NOTE: No user-authen-restriction is configured."
          solution    : "Configuring the number of failures and locking time by running the following commands:

          ZXR10 (config)#system-user
          ZXR10 (config-system-user)#user-authen-restriction fail-time 3 lock-minute 2"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </else>
    </if>

# 7.4 (1.4) SNMP Security

    <if>
      <condition type:"OR">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Check if SNMP server v1 has been enabled"
          cmd         : "show running-config snmp all"
          expect      : "snmp-server version v1 enable"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Check if SNMP server v2c has been enabled"
          cmd         : "show running-config snmp all"
          expect      : "snmp-server version v2c enable"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.4 SNMP Security - a) SNMP Community Security"
          info        : "Both SNMP version 1 and SNMP version 2 are insecure. If SNMP is required, SNMP version 3 should be configured.

          NOTE: snmp-server version 1 and/or snmp-server version 2 have/has been configured."
          solution    : "If SNMP is required, ZTE Router Platform should be configured for SNMP version 3 only.

          Configuring SNMP version 3 by running the following commands:

          ZXR10 # configure terminal
          ZXR10 (config)#snmp-server version v3 enable"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>

        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.4 SNMP Security - b) SNMP Security Protection Function"
          info        : "Enable the SNMP security function to restrict the number of times of management address, prevent hackers from malicious attacks, and improve the security of ROSNG series products.

          NOTE: snmp-server version 1 and/or snmp-server version 2 have/has been configured."
          solution    : "(a) Disable snmp-server version 1 and/or snmp-server version 2
          ZXR10 (config)#no snmp-server version v1
          ZXR10 (config)#no snmp-server version v2c

          (b) Enable security protection:

          ZXR10 (config)#snmp-server security block 200  15 100 when 10 60"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <if>
          <condition type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type        : CMD_EXEC
              description : "Check if SNMP server v3 has been enabled"
              cmd         : "show running-config snmp all"
              expect      : "snmp-server version v3 enable"
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.4 SNMP Security - a) SNMP Community Security"
              info        : "Both SNMP version 1 and SNMP version 2 are insecure. If SNMP is required, SNMP version 3 should be configured.

              NOTE: snmp-server version v3 is enabled."
              solution    : "If SNMP is required, ZTE Router Platform should be configured for SNMP version 3 only.

              Configuring SNMP version 3 by running the following commands:

              ZXR10 # configure terminal
              ZXR10 (config)#snmp-server version v3 enable"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>

            <custom_item>
              type        : CMD_EXEC
              description : "1.4 SNMP Security - b) SNMP Security Protection Function"
              info        : "Enable the SNMP security function to restrict the number of times of management address, prevent hackers from malicious attacks, and improve the security of ROSNG series products."
              solution    : "Enable security protection:

              ZXR10 (config)#snmp-server security block 200  15 100 when 10 60"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              cmd         : "show running-config snmp all"
              expect      : "^snmp-server security block .+"
            </custom_item>
          </then>

          <else>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.4 SNMP Security - a) SNMP Community Security"
              info        : "Both SNMP version 1 and SNMP version 2 are insecure. If SNMP is required, SNMP version 3 should be configured.

              NOTE: No snmp-server configuration has been detected."
              solution    : "If SNMP is required, ZTE Router Platform should be configured for SNMP version 3 only.

              Configuring SNMP version 3 by running the following commands:

              ZXR10 # configure terminal
              ZXR10 (config)#snmp-server version v3 enable"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>

            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.4 SNMP Security - b) SNMP Security Protection Function"
              info        : "NOTE: No snmp-server configuration has been detected."
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </else>
        </if>
      </else>
    </if>

# 7.5 (1.5) FTP/SFTP Access Authorization

    <if>
      <condition type:"OR">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Check for if ftp-server is enabled"
          cmd         : "show running-config ftp all"
          expect      : "^ftp-server enable"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Check for if ftp-secure-server is enabled"
          cmd         : "show running-config ftp all"
          expect      : "^ftp-secure-server enable"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.5 FTP/SFTP Access Authorization - login-type-allowed"
          info        : "Set ftp upload and download file permission control to facilitate the separate control of different users and different permissions, and strengthen the security of ZTE Router Platform series products.

          NOTE: ftp-server enable and/or ftp-secure-server has been configured."
          solution    : "Close the ftp access channel, for example:

          ZXR10 (config)# no ftp-server enable
          ZXR10 (config)# sftp-server enable
          ZXR10 (config-system-user-author-temp)# login-type-allowed ssh."
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>

        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.5 FTP/SFTP Access Authorization - sftp top-directory"
          info        : "Set ftp upload and download file permission control to facilitate the separate control of different users and different permissions, and strengthen the security of ZTE Router Platform series products.

          NOTE: ftp-server enable and/or ftp-secure-server has been configured."
          solution    : "(a)To disable ftp-server and/or ftp-secure-server
          ZXR10(config)# no ftp-server enable
          ZXR10(config)# ftp-secure-server disable

          (b) Under authorization-template, configure the corresponding ftp permissions, such as:

          ZXR10 (config)#sftp-server top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only

          OR

          ZXR10 (config-system-user-author-temp) #sftp top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <if>
          <condition type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type        : CMD_EXEC
              description : "Check for if sftp-server is enabled"
              cmd         : "show running-config sftp all"
              expect      : "sftp-server enable"
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.5 FTP/SFTP Access Authorization - login-type-allowed"
              info        : "Set ftp upload and download file permission control to facilitate the separate control of different users and different permissions, and strengthen the security of ZTE Router Platform series products.

              NOTE: sftp-server is enable. No ftp server configuration has been detected."
              solution    : "Close the ftp access channel, for example:

              ZXR10 (config)# no ftp-server enable
              ZXR10 (config)# sftp-server enable
              ZXR10 (config-system-user-author-temp)# login-type-allowed ssh."
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>

            <if>
              <condition type:"OR">
                <custom_item>
                  type        : CMD_EXEC
                  description : "sftp-server top-directory"
                  cmd         : "show running-config sftp all"
                  expect      : ".*sftp-server top-directory .+"
                </custom_item>

                <custom_item>
                  type        : CMD_EXEC
                  description : "sftp top-directory"
                  cmd         : "show running-config system-user"
                  expect      : ".*sftp top-directory .+"
                </custom_item>
              </condition>

              <then>
                <report type:"PASSED">
                  description : "1.5 FTP/SFTP Access Authorization - sftp top-directory"
                  info        : "Set ftp upload and download file permission control to facilitate the separate control of different users and different permissions, and strengthen the security of ZTE Router Platform series products.

                  NOTE: sftp-server is enable and sftp top-directory is configured."
                  solution    : "Under authorization-template, configure the corresponding ftp permissions, such as:

                  ZXR10 (config)#sftp-server top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only

                  OR

                  ZXR10 (config-system-user-author-temp) #sftp top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only"
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>
              </then>

              <else>
                <report type:"FAILED">
                  description : "1.5 FTP/SFTP Access Authorization - sftp top-directory"
                  info        : "Set ftp upload and download file permission control to facilitate the separate control of different users and different permissions, and strengthen the security of ZTE Router Platform series products.

                  NOTE: sftp-server is enable. sftp top-directory is not configured."
                  solution    : "Under authorization-template, configure the corresponding ftp permissions, such as:

                  ZXR10(config)#sftp-server top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only

                  OR

                  ZXR10 (config-system-user-author-temp) #sftp top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only"
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>
              </else>
            </if>
          </then>

          <else>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.5 FTP/SFTP Access Authorization - login-type-allowed"
              info        : "Set ftp upload and download file permission control to facilitate the separate control of different users and different permissions, and strengthen the security of ZTE Router Platform series products.

              NOTE: No ftp/sftp server configuration has been detected."
              solution    : "Close the ftp access channel, for example:

              ZXR10 (config)# no ftp-server enable
              ZXR10 (config)# sftp-server enable
              ZXR10 (config-system-user-author-temp)# login-type-allowed ssh."
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>

            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.5 FTP/SFTP Access Authorization - sftp top-directory"
              info        : "Set ftp upload and download file permission control to facilitate the separate control of different users and different permissions, and strengthen the security of ZTE Router Platform series products.

              NOTE: No ftp/sftp server configuration has been detected."
              solution    : "Under authorization-template, configure the corresponding ftp permissions, such as:

              ZXR10 (config)#sftp-server top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only

              OR

              ZXR10 (config-system-user-author-temp) #sftp top-directory /datadisk0/ read-only"
              see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </else>
        </if>
      </else>
    </if>

# 7.6 (1.6) Support Web Access Security

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Check if web server is configured"
          cmd         : "show running-config web all"
          expect      : "web server enable"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - a) ciphersuite"
          info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

          NOTE: web server enable is configured. Check on ciphersuite was not carried out."
          solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate
          2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
          3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5"
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>

        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - b) ssl-context field"
          info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

          NOTE: web server enable is configured. Check on ssl-context field was not carried out."
          solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
          2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
          3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>

        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - c) version"
          info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

          NOTE: web server enable is configured. Check on version was not carried out."
          solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
          2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
          3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
          see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <if>
          <condition type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type        : CMD_EXEC
              description : "Check if web secure-server is configured"
              cmd         : "show running-config web all"
              expect      : "web secure-server enable"
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <if>
              <condition type:"AND">
                <custom_item>
                  type        : CMD_EXEC
                  description : "Check if web secure-server ssl context is configured"
                  cmd         : "show running-config web all"
                  expect      : "web secure-server ssl-context .+"
                </custom_item>
              </condition>

              <then>
                <custom_item>
                  type        : CMD_EXEC
                  description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - a) ciphersuite"
                  info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

                  NOTE: web secure-server and ssl-context are configured."
                  solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
                  2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
                  3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  cmd         : "show running-config ssl all"
                  not_expect  : ".*ciphersuite.+((-md5 |-sha |-cbc-sha )|(-md5$|-sha$|-cbc-sha$))"
                </custom_item>

                <report type:"PASSED">
                  description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - b) ssl-context field"
                  info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

                  NOTE: web secure-server and ssl-context are configured."
                  solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
                  2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
                  3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>

                <custom_item>
                  type        : CMD_EXEC
                  description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - c) version"
                  info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

                  NOTE: web secure-server and ssl-context are configured."
                  solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
                  2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
                  3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  cmd         : "show running-config ssl all"
                  expect      : ".*version.*(tls(1.2|1.3)|gm1.1)"
                </custom_item>
              </then>

              <else>
                <report type:"FAILED">
                  description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - a) ciphersuite"
                  info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

                  NOTE: web secure-server and/or ssl-context is not configured. Check on ciphersuite was not carried out."
                  solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
                  2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
                  3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>

                <report type:"FAILED">
                  description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - b) ssl-context field"
                  info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

                  NOTE: web secure-server and/or ssl-context is not configured."
                  solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
                  2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
                  3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>

                <report type:"FAILED">
                  description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - c) version"
                  info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

                  NOTE: web secure-server and/or ssl-context is not configured. Check on version was not carried out."
                  solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
                  2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
                  3.	TLS algorithm does not contain insecure algorithms, which include: CBC, SHA1, MD5."
                  see_also    : "https://support.zte.com.cn/support/doccenter/DocumentProductHandBookDetail.aspx?sid=102&id=30768582&type=docfeedback"
                  show_output : YES
                </report>
              </else>
            </if>
          </then>

          <else>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.6 Support Web Access Security - a) ciphersuite"
              info        : "Provide secure HTTPS webpage access between the local device and users, and a secure transmission channel for users' Web management devices. Avoid interception of intermediate data. If the login page needs to be displayed in the web, the login username and password can be used to access the page, meeting the scanning requirements of security tools such as nessus, webinspect, and AWE.

              NOTE: No web server and web secure-server configuration has been detected."
              solution    : "1.	use HTTPS instead of HTTP, SSL must bound PKI profile, the bounded PKI profile needs to import a legal and valid CA certificate.
              2.	TLS(SSL) version is recommended to be equal or greater than TLS v1.2.
